cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GloriPaka, please cite it as below."
title: "GloriPaka: sequence-based HIC-retention prediction for VHH nanobodies"
abstract: >-
  GloriPaka predicts hydrophobic-interaction-chromatography (HIC) retention for
  VHH single-domain antibodies (nanobodies) from sequence, via predicted 3-D
  structure and transferable surface-hydrophobicity biophysics combined with a
  leakage-free machine-learning ensemble.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GloriusGroup/GloriPaka"
authors:
  - family-names: Boser
    given-names: Florian
  - name: "Glorius Group, University of Münster"
keywords:
  - VHH
  - nanobody
  - HIC
  - developability
  - machine learning
  - antibody
